"link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 6421, "created": 1790960831000, "id": "2106068488515448983", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1345865078755627010/Msxww2jO_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Governor Greg Gianforte", "username": "GovGianforte"}, "content": "I am excited to announce I will be leading a delegation to India and Sri Lanka. \n\nJoining over 30 Montanans in country, we will showcase our world-class products, build on longstanding relationships, and open new doors for Montana businesses, universities, and producers.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 1152}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVVeiFQl", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 23, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8869167, "raw_content": "This post is not accusatory. I just wanted to ask because a lot of republican voters feel this way. Despite what republican influencers or republican news sources say, I believe the biggest betrayal in the lifetime of the republican party's history is this:\n\n * Senate Majority Leader John Thune declined to change Senate rules for bypassing the 60-vote threshold to pass President Donald Trump's SAVE America Act\n\nTo me, the only other time I felt like this in my entire life was when we all learned that John Roberts (the chief justice, appointed by president Bush) was the tie-breaker vote who gave us Obamacare or learning the John McCain was the tiebreaker vote against repealing \"the affordable care act\". Along with Susan Collins and Lisa Murkowski who I never knew about until a couple minutes ago -- I thought McCain was the only republican who voted against repealing Obamacare -- so I have updated my first paragraph accordingly.\n\n**TL;DR:** There are many republicans who feel betrayed by the politicians on our side of the aisle (including but not limited to Thune, Randy Fine, etc). I wanted to politely ask for for the reason someone who feels betrayed should vote Republican in the upcoming midterm elections rather than voting 3rd party (i.e. wasting their vote in protest on a candidate who has no possible chance of winning).", "author": "InternetSolutions", "created": 1791077752038, "profile_picture": "WfZMn2HAZgiW", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "InternetSolutions", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "There are many republicans who feel betrayed by the politicians on our side of the aisle (including but not limited to Thune, Randy Fine, etc). I wanted to politely ask for for the reason someone who feels betrayed should vote Republican rather than 3rd party (i.e. wasting their vote in protest) ", "last_comment_created": 1791085782229, "content": "<p>This post is not accusatory. I just wanted to ask because a lot of republican voters feel this way. Despite what republican influencers or republican news sources say, I believe the biggest betrayal in the lifetime of the republican party's history is this:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Senate Majority Leader John Thune declined to change Senate rules for bypassing the 60-vote threshold to pass President Donald Trump's SAVE America Act</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To me, the only other time I felt like this in my entire life was when we all learned that John Roberts (the chief justice, appointed by president Bush) was the tie-breaker vote who gave us Obamacare or learning the John McCain was the tiebreaker vote against repealing &quot;the affordable care act&quot;. Along with Susan Collins and Lisa Murkowski who I never knew about until a couple minutes ago -- I thought McCain was the only republican who voted against repealing Obamacare -- so I have updated my first paragraph accordingly.</p>\n<p><strong>TL;DR:</strong> There are many republicans who feel betrayed by the politicians on our side of the aisle (including but not limited to Thune, Randy Fine, etc). I wanted to politely ask for for the reason someone who feels betrayed should vote Republican in the upcoming midterm elections rather than voting 3rd party (i.e. wasting their vote in protest on a candidate who has no possible chance of winning).</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 14, "score_up": 23, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVVdaxAe", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 115, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8868570, "raw_content": "", "author": "Beat_to_Quarters", "created": 1791046123405, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "45fan", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATVVdaxAe.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/e9mOK3Xs3seE.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/gWSNuKPp1pL0nwRU.jpeg", "width": 720, "content-type": "jpeg", "height": 702}], "blurhash": "UPRC;~Rk~qxaxZs:R+RjD%R*%Mt6?bofM{Rk", "full_resolution": [702, 720]}, "title": "When activist judges rule the constitution is unconstitutional, what's left to do at this point? \ud83d\ude14", "last_comment_created": 1791067065668, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_